{
 "note": "Two halves on purpose, in the grammar of the iPhone 5C campaign: 24 clips of a phone actually in someone's hand, and 12 flat fields of saturated colour to cut between them. Colour block, product, colour block.",
 "made_by": {
  "how": "curated",
  "who": "a person looking at a contact sheet of 90 phone/hand/colour clips",
  "not": "Green-screen plates were excluded -- clips 04, 53 and 69 are compositing material and read as a flat green rectangle if used raw.",
  "why": "The previous ad was cut from hands typing, bokeh and smoke in a dark room, which has nothing to do with a phone. The words in that brief were ones the POOL could satisfy rather than ones the ad needed."
 },
